        "original_id": "8ec86a65-cfa6-5a7d-8a95-55b2146a387e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Arnold, Raymond A. Palmer\n- Places: Mount Rainier, Washington, Cascade Range, United States\n- Events: World UFO Day, 1947 Roswell UFO Incident, Kenneth Arnold sighting\n- Products: The Coming of the Saucers\n- Topics: unidentified flying objects, flying saucers\n\nFacts:\n- On June 24, 1947, Kenneth Arnold reported seeing nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington, in what is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States.\n- July 2 is observed by World UFO Day to commemorate the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\n- Mount Rainier, in Washington in the Cascade Range, is the highest peak in the range at 14,411 feet.\n- Raymond A. Palmer co-wrote the flying saucer book \"The Coming of the Saucers\" with Kenneth Arnold.\n- Raymond A. Palmer also published magazines including \"Mystic,\" \"Search,\" and \"Flying Saucers,\" along with numerous spiritualist books.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a4cd0716-c9fb-50bc-98db-316e134a8264",
        "text": "Page: World UFO Day. Sentence: June 24 is the date that aviator Kenneth Arnold reported what is generally considered to be the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States, while July 2 commemorates the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\nPage: Kenneth Arnold. Sentence: He is best known for making what is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States, after claiming to have seen nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington on June 24, 1947.\nPage: Raymond A. Palmer. Sentence: In addition to magazines such as \"Mystic,\" \"Search,\" and 'Flying Saucers,\" he published numerous spirtualist books, including \"\", as well as several books related to flying saucers, including \"The Coming of the Saucers,\" co-written by Palmer with Kenneth Arnold.\nPage: Cascade Range. Sentence: The highest peak in the range is Mount Rainier in Washington at 14411 ft .",
